'' A FIXED-LENGTH STRING OFFERED { byref const string, byref string } IS AMBIGUOUS -- fbc's
'' error 98 on lines 7 and 8, on fbc-modern 1.20, fbc 1.10.1 and fbc-modern's Linux build
'' alike (2026-09-19). Both are the same conversion and fbc asks CONST only of a same-type
'' match; tiko costed them equal too, but reported a tie only for a builtin or pointer
'' argument, and a 'zstring * 8' is an array type here -- so it ran the chain's head
'' silently. A STRING (line 9) is an exact match for 'byref string' and resolves.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/fixstr-ambiguous.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: fixstr-ambiguous.bas(7,2): error TKO0660: the call to 'g' matches more than one overload
'' EXPECT-OUT: fixstr-ambiguous.bas(8,2): error TKO0660: the call to 'g' matches more than one overload
